enchilada: GPU: cacheable client mappings of arena BOs, maintained by the kernel

CPU access to GPU buffers ran at about 50 MB/s (a 1024x1024 readback: 84.5 ms a frame, 20 ms per
MiB). The libdrm stand-in maps every BO with IOConnectMapMemory64(conn, handle, task, &addr,
&size, 0x401) (sweet_drm_mmap: mov w5, #0x401 = kIOMapAnywhere | kIOMapWriteCombineCache), and
IOUserClient::mapClientMemory64() replaces the driver's cache bits with the client's
(options & ~kIOMapUserOptionsMask | mapFlags & kIOMapUserOptionsMask). clientMemoryForType()
returned 0, the withPhysicalAddress() descriptor's memory entry is copyback (the arena pages are
pa_valid with no WIMG attribute: VM_WIMG_DEFAULT), and memoryReferenceMap() then re-types the
entry to VM_WIMG_WCOMB - Normal non-cacheable, so every CPU load goes to DRAM. Now arena BOs ask
for kIOMapCopybackCache, and mapClientMemory64() keeps a cache mode the driver names (no other
user client in this kernel sets one). Coherency is the kernel's job, by physical address with
flush_dcache64(pa, len, TRUE) (dc civac through the static aperture, which covers the arena;
dcache_incoherent_io_flush64() is not used: above c_bulksize_op it does a set/way flush, wrong on
SMP). SUBMIT cleans every BO as before, but before the relocation patch (a dirty client line
written back afterwards would undo a patch stored through the uncached window) and cleans each
patched command range after it (aperture stores are cached). Every BO of a submission is marked
GPU-dirty; CPU_PREP (READ or WRITE, after its wait or a NOSYNC check) and a successful WAIT_FENCE
clean+invalidate GPU-dirty BOs whose submissions are done, so the CPU neither hits nor merges into
stale lines (Mesa skips CPU_PREP when its own fence word says idle, hence WAIT_FENCE too).
CPU_FINI cleans the BO, BO_SYNC cleans+invalidates the range by pa, and GEM_CLOSE
cleans+invalidates the BO before its pages go back to the arena. IOSurface BOs keep the client's
mode. One boot line names the mode; sweetbocache=0 gives the client's own mode back (write-combined).

